     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br>I&#39;m afraid I&#39;m next to Geomorph so my questions are quite basic:<br><ol><li>My project involves measuring lengths/angles/ratios between various landmarks on photographs of (live) horse&#39;s feet, which seems to be different from what most other people use this for but presumably it should still work?</li><li>I have tried to follow instructions on importing photos and digitising them in 2D but just get a load of error images (see below). I was wondering if anyone has any example code that I could use to get started, or recommendations of tutorials?</li><li>We are taking photographs from the front, the side and underneath the hoof, is is possible to use these views to create 3D images using Geomorph?</li></ol><p>Thanks in advance,</p><p>Sarah</p><p><br></p><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">setwd(&quot;C:/Users/sarahh88/Pictures/2d_midpaleolithic_specs&quot;)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">specs&lt;-list.files()[grep(&quot;.JPG&quot;,list.files())]\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">specs\r\n</span>[1] &quot;spec100.JPG&quot; &quot;spec143.JPG&quot; &quot;spec164.JPG&quot;\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">source(url(&quot;<a href=\"http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486100333000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rx9xFX-b2PBqxp3N6wGvF\">http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R</a>&quot;))\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">diged.imgs &lt;- lapply(specs, digitize2d.multi, nlandmarks=3, scale=1)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in FUN(X[[i]], ...) : could not find function &quot;digitize2d&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">Loading required package: jpeg\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error: unexpected symbol in &quot;Loading required&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">set scale = 1\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error: unexpected symbol in &quot;set scale&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">diged.imgs &lt;- lapply(specs, digitize2d.multi, nlandmarks=3, scale=1)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in FUN(X[[i]], ...) : could not find function &quot;digitize2d&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">View(digitize2d.multi)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">diged.imgs&lt;-lapply(specs, digitize2d.multi, nlandmarks=3,scale=1)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in FUN(X[[i]], ...) : could not find function &quot;digitize2d&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In addition: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">closing unused connection 3 (<a href=\"http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486100333000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rx9xFX-b2PBqxp3N6wGvF\">http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R</a>) \r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(geomorph)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Loading required package: rgl\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Loading required package: ape\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">package ‘geomorph’ was built under R version 3.3.3 \r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">setwd(&quot;C:/Users/sarahh88/Pictures/2d_midpaleolithic_specs&quot;)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">specs&lt;-list.files()[grep(&quot;.JPG&quot;,list.files())]\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">specs\r\n</span>[1] &quot;spec100.JPG&quot; &quot;spec143.JPG&quot; &quot;spec164.JPG&quot;\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">source(url(&quot;<a href=\"http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486100333000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rx9xFX-b2PBqxp3N6wGvF\">http://www.people.fas.harvard.edu/~eotarolacastillo/software/digitze2dmulti.R</a>&quot;))\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">diged.imgs &lt;- lapply(specs, digitize2d.multi, nlandmarks=3, scale=1)\r\n</span><div style=\"overflow:hidden;margin:5px 5px 5px 0px;padding:5px 0px 5px 5px;background-color:rgb(229,229,229)\"><div style=\"float:right;margin-right:10px;margin-left:5px;margin-bottom:15px;line-height:10px\"><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/geomorph-r-package/attach/247b7bb9f243c/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1\" width=\"9\" height=\"9\"> <a style=\"font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:11px;opacity:0.5\" rel=\"nofollow\">Hide Traceback</a></div> <div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/geomorph-r-package/attach/247b7bb9f243c/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%202?part=0.2\" width=\"9\" height=\"9\"> <a style=\"font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:11px;opacity:0.5\" rel=\"nofollow\">Rerun with Debug</a></div></div> <div style=\"display:inline;word-wrap:break-word;word-break:break-word;margin-left:0.3em;color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in which(flist == tpsfile) : \r\n  argument &quot;tpsfile&quot; is missing, with no default</div> <div style=\"margin-top:0.5em;margin-left:0.3em\"><table style=\"clear:both\"><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1.5em;text-align:right;margin-top:0.3em;white-space:nowrap;font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,205)\">4.</div></td><td style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div><div style=\"display:inline\">which(flist == tpsfile)</div> </div></td></tr></tbody></table><table style=\"clear:both\"><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1.5em;text-align:right;margin-top:0.3em;white-space:nowrap;font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,205)\">3.</div></td><td style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div><div style=\"display:inline\">digitize2d(x, nlandmarks, scale) at</div> <a style=\"color:rgb(0,0,205)\" rel=\"nofollow\">digitze2dmulti.R&quot;)#2</a></div></td></tr></tbody></table><table style=\"clear:both\"><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1.5em;text-align:right;margin-top:0.3em;white-space:nowrap;font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,205)\">2.</div></td><td style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div><div style=\"display:inline\">FUN(X[[i]], ...)</div> </div></td></tr></tbody></table><table style=\"clear:both\"><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1.5em;text-align:right;margin-top:0.3em;white-space:nowrap;font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,205)\">1.</div></td><td style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;line-height:1.2;font-size:10pt!important\"><div><div style=\"display:inline\">lapply(specs, digitize2d.multi, nlandmarks = 3, scale = 1)</div> </div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">diged.imgs &lt;- lapply(specs, digitize2d.multi, nlandmarks=3, scale=1)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in which(flist == tpsfile) : \r\n  argument &quot;tpsfile&quot; is missing, with no default\r\n</span>Called from: which(flist == tpsfile)\r\n<span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">Browse[1]&gt; </span></pre></div>"
