     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Sarah Harley<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Monday, July 3, 2017 6:44 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] 2D digitisation horse&#39;s feet<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<br>\r\nI&#39;m afraid I&#39;m next to Geomorph so my questions are quite basic:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\nMy project involves measuring lengths/angles/ratios between various landmarks on photographs of (live) horse&#39;s feet, which seems to be different from what most other people use this for but presumably it should still work?<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\nI have tried to follow instructions on importing photos and digitising them in 2D but just get a load of error images (see below). I was wondering if anyone has any example code that I could use to get started, or recommendations of tutorials?<u></u><u></u></li><li class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\nWe are taking photographs from the front, the side and underneath the hoof, is is possible to use these views to create 3D images using Geomorph?<u></u><u></u></li></ol>\r\n<p>Thanks in advance,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Sarah<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;wor